    },
    "body": "The previous bridge fits changed native actions but regressed. This adds a Rust learner that evaluates fixed legal discrete proposals on the complete native objective and accepts only strict improvements, comparing each coupled edit with its exact lane partitions.\n\nBoth source-bound pod runs complete at `6845a9c3`: 18 proposals per arm change packed coefficients but preserve all570 native decisions and CE0.492381624865. Selection retains the parent; no improved model is adopted. The new result identifies a decision-region plateau and directs the next work toward explicit native winner crossings rather than an unchanged scale sweep. Whole-prefix retrieval remains a separate coordinated attention requirement.\n\nValidation: six focused tests and optimized build pass on Linux CPU; saved-result independent review806,280 checks0errors;334 returned files140,279,133B match the complete remote SHA/file set. Claim-wording check passes. Reports qualify unavailable independent BLAKE3, omitted gradient reconstruction, Metal and broad language/energy claims. No existing runtime/library/schema changes.\n\nReferences #1552. References #820.\n",
